In article <1fimipINNfg6@early-bird.think.com>, bickford@jimmy.dfci.harvard.edu (Paul Bickford) writes:
|> Could someone tell me how to get into wizard mode? And how does one
|> access the functions when I'm in it? And what are the functions?
|> 
|> [Notes: Nethack 3.0j, PC version. Tried "nethack -uname -w" and
|> "nethack -uname wizard" and neither worked. Or, more appropriately,
|> tried it and could not see any difference: no extra commands were
|> listed, etc.]
|> 

try: netachk -u Wizard -D

(I assume that -u and -uname are the same, I know this works)

-u sets your name to be Wizard
-D play in wizard mode.

To get the list of commands, type '?'.  Wizard's get an extra item in the menu
that lists all the commands.


